        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "meteorology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Meteorology - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The atmosphere is a thin fluid shell (99% of mass below 30 km; Earth's radius is 6,371 km) driven by differential solar heating and shaped by Earth's rotation. Weather is the short-term state; climate is the long-term statistics. All of meteorology follows from fluid dynamics + thermodynamics applied to a rotating, stratified fluid on a sphere."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#003",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:meteorology:00-overview, git-history:meteorology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "meteorology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "meteorology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:meteorology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "meteorology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "meteorology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Meteorology - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                    ATMOSPHERE AS A SYSTEM                        |\n|                                                                  |\n|  ENERGY IN: Solar radiation (short-wave)                         |\n|  ENERGY OUT: Longwave infrared + reflected short-wave            |\n|                                                                  |\n|  CIRCULATION ENGINES:                                            |\n|  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐         |\n|  │ Differential heating (equator hot, poles cold)      │         |\n|  │    ↓                                                │         |\n|  │ Pressure gradients + Coriolis deflection            │         |\n|  │    ↓                                                │         |\n|  │ Hadley/Ferrel/Polar cells (mean circulation)        │         |\n|  │    ↓                                                │         |\n|  │ Jet streams, Rossby waves (synoptic variability)    │         |\n|  │    ↓                                                │         |\n|  │ Frontal systems, cyclones (weather systems)         │         |\n|  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘         |\n|                                                                   |\n|  WATER CYCLE: Evaporation → Condensation → Precipitation        |\n|  (latent heat release = primary driver of thunderstorms)         |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
